hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"37","On lightening the prayer. Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him measure the prayer by the weakest among them, for behind him are the old, the weak, the needy, the sick, and the one far from home."
"38","Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abbas al-Jushami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the imams are drivers-away. Qatadah said: I know the drivers-away to be none but those who lengthen the prayer over the people until they drive them away from it."
"39","Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Sawda, from Ibn Sabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer and recited sixty verses, then heard the voice of a child, so he bowed; then he stood, recited two verses, then bowed."
